<header class="page-head">
	<div class="wrap">
		<p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
		<h1>What runs where, and who may do what.</h1>
		<p class="lead">Sub-Sub runs on your computer. The model and the literature services are online. The mode decides what Sub-Sub works on; the profile decides how much it writes for you; every library change waits for your Yes.</p>
	</div>
</header>

<section class="section" id="what-runs-where">
	<div class="wrap">
		<p class="eyebrow">How it fits together</p>
		<h2>What runs where.</h2>
		<p class="section-lead">Everything except the model and the online services runs on your computer. The mode decides which servers Sub-Sub may use: the Librarian uses zotero only, the Researcher uses zotero, scholar and verify. The profile removes tools from what is left.</p>
		{% include "diagram.njk" %}
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
	<div class="wrap">
		<p class="eyebrow">Two modes</p>
		<h2>The Researcher does everything. The Librarian only keeps the library.</h2>
		<p class="section-lead">The Researcher is the default: research a topic and file what you find in the same conversation. Use the Librarian for tagging sessions with a fast, cheap model.</p>
		<div class="modes">
			<article class="mode researcher">
				<h3>Researcher</h3>
				<p class="mode-lead">Reads your library and the literature, and changes the library too.</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Answers "what do I have on…?" from your library, with citekeys.</li>
					<li>Searches PubMed, Europe PMC and OpenAlex for works that are not in your library.</li>
					<li>Writes literature notes, syntheses and literature reviews with a screening log. Each note says what Sub-Sub read: the full text, the abstract or only the metadata.</li>
					<li>Checks the references of a manuscript with Starbuck, an optional add-on.</li>
					<li>Imports, tags and repairs what it finds, with a preview for each change.</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="mode-cmds"><code>/lit</code> <code>/lit-note</code> <code>/synthesis</code> <code>/gaps</code> <code>/compare</code> <code>/verify</code> <code>/researcher</code></p>
			</article>
			<article class="mode librarian">
				<h3>Librarian</h3>
				<p class="mode-lead">Manages the library only.</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Tags items with the tags in your own list, <code>Zotero/Zotero tags.md</code>. It refuses other tags.</li>
					<li>Writes tag proposals into a review note that you can edit before you apply it.</li>
					<li>Imports by DOI, PMID or ISBN, with the abstract and a citekey.</li>
					<li>Repairs metadata, finds duplicates, flags retractions and attaches open-access PDFs.</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="mode-cmds"><code>/tag-batch</code> <code>/clean-tags</code> <code>/import-queue</code> <code>/history</code> <code>/undo</code> <code>/librarian</code></p>
			</article>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
	<div class="wrap split terminal-split">
		<div>
			<p class="eyebrow">Browser or terminal</p>
			<h2>The same Sub-Sub in both.</h2>
			<p>Open Sub-Sub from its shortcut and it opens in your browser. Type <code>subsub</code> and it opens in the terminal. The modes, the profiles and the approvals are the same.</p>
			<p>The browser view is a small server on your own computer. It listens only on 127.0.0.1 and stops 10 minutes after you close the page.</p>
		</div>
<div class="terminal" role="img" aria-label="Sub-Sub in the terminal: it shows a preview of a tag change and asks Yes or No.">
<pre><span class="t-dim">$</span> subsub --librarian
<span class="t-acc">Sub-Sub {{ release.version }}</span>  <span class="t-dim">Librarian, Scholar · Zotero: 1,024 items</span>

<span class="t-acc">&gt;</span> Tag the next 10 items without a topic.</pre>
<div class="t-box"><span class="t-box-title">Sub-Sub: apply tag_items?</span>
<pre>2 item(s) would change.
Smith 2021: Home spirometry in children with asthma
  <span class="t-add">+ topic/respiratory, topic/pediatrics, type/cohort</span>
Costa 2019: A decision aid for inhaler choice
  <span class="t-add">+ topic/clinical-decision-support</span>; <span class="t-rem">- type/rct</span></pre>
<span class="t-box-keys"><span class="t-on">Yes</span> <span class="t-dim">No</span></span></div>
</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
	<div class="wrap split">
		<div>
			<p class="eyebrow">What you need</p>
			<h2>Three things. The installer does the rest.</h2>
		</div>
		<dl class="needs">
			<div><dt>Zotero 10 or later</dt><dd>Running, with "Allow other applications on this computer to communicate with Zotero" on.</dd></div>
			<div><dt>An account with a model provider</dt><dd>Any provider that pi supports, or a local model. See <a href="/models/">Models</a> for the tested ones.</dd></div>
			<div><dt>A place for notes</dt><dd>Sub-Sub keeps its Markdown notes in one folder, Sub-Sub. It can sit inside your Obsidian vault.</dd></div>
		</dl>
	</div>
</section>